        "blast_url": "https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi?PAGE_TYPE=BlastSearch&PROG_DEF=blastn&BLAST_SPEC=GDH_GCA_984573615.1",
        "comments": "The assembly dmFumMura2.hap1.1 is based on 78x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The species looks to be highly heterozygous and some haplotypic inversions were detected on: Chromosome 1 HAP1 3.82 Mbp - 8.58 Mbp and HAP3 3.25 Mbp - 8.07 Mbp. Chromosome 2 HAP1 9.03 Mbp - 11.15 Mbp and HAP3 6.28 Mbp - 8.33 Mbp. Chromosome 3 HAP1 6.74 Mbp - 16.65 Mbp, 20.12 Mbp - 22.81 Mbp, HAP2 6.60 Mbp - 15.29 Mbp, 17.69 Mbp - 19.71 Mbp and HAP3 6.48 Mbp - 14.75 Mbp , 15.12 Mbp - 19.14 Mbp. Chromosome 5 HAP1 7.53 Mbp - 9.48 Mbp, HAP2 6.66 Mbp - 8.66 Mbp and HAP3 5.43 Mbp - 6.46 Mbp. Chromosome 6 HAP1 3.54 Mbp - 7.28 Mbp, 17.30 Mbp - 18.73 Mbp, HAP2 2.77 Mbp - 7.39 Mbp, 14.61 Mbp - 15.43 Mbp, HAP3 4.78 Mbp - 6.71 Mbp, 13.82 Mbp - 14.83 Mbp. Chromosome 8 HAP1 8.38 Mbp - 13.68 Mbp, HAP2 5.55 Mbp - 10.11 Mbp and HAP3 4.48 Mbp - 9.96 Mbp. As we could not identify the potential recombining chromosomes based on the HiC signal, all 3 haplotypes were curated.",
